 "scale_warning": "These counts are one to two orders of magnitude larger than the downtown street counts (SD CoC ~10,605 in 2024 vs. downtown monthly totals in the hundreds). Plot on a secondary axis or as a separate indexed series; a shared linear axis will flatten the downtown line to zero.",
 "caveats": {
  "2021": "HUD permitted CoCs to skip the unsheltered count during COVID. The source data marks San Diego's 2021 row Count Types = 'Sheltered-Only Count' (every other year is 'Sheltered and Unsheltered Count'), so 2021 is not comparable to the rest of the series. Use the per-year count_type / methodology_break fields rather than hardcoding the year. Break or annotate the line; never interpolate across it.",
  "cadence": "One observation per year, taken on a single night in late January."
 },
